                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The music and art are beautiful as always, as expected of a Trine game.\nI really like the Trine series and I played this game already knowing it was going to have a bunch of issues. And there are plenty:\n- The departure from sidescrolling platforming to 3D platforming didn't do the game any good. I missed jumps constantly and often died to ravines that I didn't even know were there. Aiming arrows is awkard. Sometimes the camera angle moves and then your buttons suddenly don't do what I expect them to do. And all that for an extra dimension that really doesn't add anything I feel the series needed.\n- The game is quite short and only has 3 bosses.\n- There are no upgrades to unlock. This also means that the puzzle variety is not that high and hardly changes in difficulty.\n- I ran into a whole bunch of little bugs and issues in my one playthrough.\n- You are being showered with checkpoints, even though the game isn't hard at all.\n- Trine stories have never been super deep, but this one is unfinished and ends on a cliffhanger.\n\nGo play one of the other Trine games and skip this one, unless you are a huge fan of the series.\n",
